      "content": "That \"proof-of-concept\" angle sounds good, but even then, reviewers are usually pretty brutal about power analysis and statistical validity. If we lean too hard into the \"high-resolution\" thing, won't they just see it as a way to mask the fact that the results might be due to chance? Like, is there a risk we're being a bit too optimistic about how much weight this data can actually carry?",
